# fleet-ops#146 (storm-tolerant panel): CPU/Memory ceiling for every
# pi-audit@* senior-auditor instance. An intake burst that fires 42
# audit units in parallel (14 scout-candidate issues * 3 roles) drove
# load to 49 on a 8-vCPU host on 2026-08-27 and starved the intake
# loop's agent-ready lane. The per-tick spawn cap (TICK_MAX_START in
# bin/fleet-heartbeat-auditor) is the FIRST guard; this slice is the
# SECOND guard so a long-running cohort of audit units cannot exceed
# the host's reasonable share.
#
# 300% CPUQuota = 3 cores; audits are oneshot and mostly network-bound,
# so 3 cores lets ~3 run at full speed while the rest throttle on
# CFS. MemoryMax=4G is a safety belt (one vote packet is small, but a
# runaway 14-issue fan-out could otherwise OOM the box).
#
# Drop-in-removable: delete this file + the pi-audit@.service.d drop-in
# and daemon-reload to revert. The MANIFEST line keeps the install
# idempotent.
[Slice]
CPUQuota=300%
MemoryMax=4G
